  "claim": "A singer has released more solo albums than the singer who Avril Lavigne featured on the song Get Over Me with. This singer co-wrote \"What Were You Thinkin'\"",
  "evidencia": "Page: Nick Carter (musician). Sentence: Nickolas Gene \"Nick\" Carter (born January 28, 1980) is an American singer, songwriter, actor, and dancer.\nPage: Nick Carter (musician). Sentence: As of 2015, Carter has released three solo albums, \"Now or Never\", \"I'm Taking Off\" and \"All American\" during breaks between Backstreet Boys schedules, and a collaboration with Jordan Knight titled \"Nick & Knight\".\nPage: Brady Seals. Sentence: Brady Seals (born March 29, 1969) is an American country music artist.\nPage: Brady Seals. Sentence: A fourth solo album, \"Play Time\", was released in 2009 via Star City.\nPage: Get Over Me. Sentence: \"Get Over Me\" is a song by American singer and songwriter Nick Carter featuring Canadian singer Avril Lavigne.\nPage: What Were You Thinkin'. Sentence: The song was written by Porter Howell, Dwayne O'Brien, Brady Seals and Christy DiNapoli.",
